  "completion": "Let's break down the information given in the question and solve it step by step:\n\n1. The bear needs to gain 1000 pounds to prepare for hibernation.\n\n2. During summer, the bear gained a fifth of the weight it needed:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Weight gained from berries} = \\frac{1}{5} \\times 1000 = 200 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n\n3. Determine the total weight gained from berries and acorns:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total weight gained} = \\text{Weight from berries} + \\text{Weight from acorns}\n   \\]\n\n4. The summer gained 200 pounds from berries, and the weight from acorns is twice what was gained from berries:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Weight from acorns} = 2 \\times 200 = 400 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n   Thus,\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total weight gained} = 200 + 400 = 600 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n\n5. Salmon accounted for half of the remaining weight the bear needed:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Weight remaining} = 1000 - 600 = 400 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n   Salmon gain:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Weight from salmon} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 400 = 200 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n\n6. Subtract the weight from salmon from the total remaining weight to get the weight gained from small animals:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Weight from small animals} = \\text{Remaining weight} - \\text{Weight from salmon}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Weight from small animals} = 400 - 200 = 200 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n\nSo, the bear gained 200 pounds eating small animals.\n\n#### 200",
  "ended_with_eos": true,
  "predicted_answer": "200",
  "question": "A bear is preparing to hibernate for the winter and needs to gain 1000 pounds. At the end of summer, the bear feasts on berries and small woodland animals. During autumn, it devours acorns and salmon. It gained a fifth of the weight it needed from berries during summer, and during autumn, it gained twice that amount from acorns. Salmon made up half of the remaining weight it had needed to gain. How many pounds did it gain eating small animals?",
